1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,440
Reading A Love of Learning Daniel is reading an article about Benjamin Franklin.

2
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:12,645
Here is the article.

3
00:00:12,645 --> 00:00:17,520
Benjamin Franklin, a lifelong learner.

4
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,430
A writer, scientist, inventor and one of the founding fathers of the United States.

5
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:28,370
Benjamin Franklin was a man of many talents.

6
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:33,760
He was also one of the most famous people in the 18th century.

7
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:40,610
From a young age, Franklin's great love of learning set him apart from many others.

8
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:48,300
As one of 17 children in a big family, Franklin had only two years of education.

9
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:55,850
After that, he started working in his brother's print shop.

10
00:00:55,850 --> 00:01:04,860
Franklin stayed up very late in order to return them early the next day.

11
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:12,290
Curious about the world around him, Franklin once became interested in studying storms.

12
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:15,670
He followed the storms and did many tests.

13
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:20,570
Then he found out that storms moved from one place to another.

14
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:23,230
His findings helped predict the weather.

15
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:31,970
What's more, Franklin had a great love for science, so his countless inventions came as no surprise.

16
00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:39,350
Even in his late 70s, he invented a type of special glasses to help him see better.

17
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:46,410
Franklin did not make money from any of his inventions, but let people use them for free.

18
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:49,690
His greatness goes further than that.

19
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:56,960
As a lifelong learner, he saw learning as an exciting journey full of wonder and success.

20
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,840
This is his greatest gift to the world.
